        "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(x)}{\\pi x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
        "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(x):$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/fc06a4e63f38a315dd3944f65f871cca2dbdddee26ec268e857f79e5f4ab8848.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(x)$ is $x\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nNow, substituting $x=1$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,1}\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(x)}{\\pi x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(1)}{\\pi \\cdot (1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
